  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 227 PM MDT FRI AUG 28 2026\nConditions slowly cool and become more active through the long\nterm as a broad trough along the coast amplifies and a strong \nclosed low pressure system moves along the trough axis. As the \ntrough axis develops Monday and Tuesday, most of the area moves \ninto the deformation zone between a shortwave ridge and \nshortwave trough. This means rebounding up to seasonal averages \non Monday inside the ridge, and increased shower and \nthunderstorm chances in south central Idaho. The shortwave ridge\nmoves out Tuesday as another shortwave trough moves through, \nthis time further north and west, covering much of the forecast \narea. Temps are mostly unchanged Monday into Tuesday, but \nenhanced storm potential moves from south central Idaho over \nhigher terrain in central and southwestern Idaho as well as \neastern Oregon.\n\nTemperatures cool properly to 10 degrees below normal Wednesday \nthrough Friday as the strong closed low moves along the trough\naxis and stalls over the Oregon coast. Unsettled and gusty \nconditions are expected in the broader region, although the \nexact placement of storms/showers is still uncertain. The strong\npressure gradient aloft is likely to mix down to the surface \nahead of the low, leading to widespread gusts each afternoon \nTuesday through the extended period.",
